= Energy efficiency — Simple =

'''Energy efficiency''' means getting a useful result while using less energy.

For example, two lamps can light the same room, but one may use less electricity. That lamp delivers the same lighting service with a lower energy input.

Energy isn't destroyed in an inefficient machine. Some energy is transferred in ways that do not help with the result we wanted, often as heat. This is part of [[Energy conversion|energy conversion]].

Efficiency is not the same as using less energy overall. If people use a device much more often, total energy use can rise even if the device is more efficient.

